  "limitations": [
    "Reveal-time request-specific voter stakes are used as an earlier arrival-time capacity proxy, so the rolling state is not a literal historical replay.",
    "Only admitted pro-rata security load, not the selected excess stake, is locked.",
    "All panel units sharing a timestamp or DVM round are sequenced deterministically rather than optimized as a simultaneous batch.",
    "Observed OO settlement time is not used as the primary release clock; it can be studied as a sensitivity.",
    "Loads are fixed in UMA at each request's dispute-time conversion; the simulation does not mark active loads to a later UMA price.",
    "The rolling workload contains only the 2,438 complete linked panel units, omitting incomplete census requests and other concurrent uses of UMA stake; estimated occupancy is therefore a lower bound for that broader workload.",
    "A NegRisk event-round treats verification of its component questions as one reusable task and posts one shared reward pool.",
    "Verification costs are modeled rather than observed."
